WHERE DOES MY WATER COME FROM?
------------------------------
Source: Cedar River (surface water) via the Cedar River Intake Pump Station
(PS-1). The state's 2017 Source Water Assessment rated the Cedar River as
MODERATELY susceptible to contamination (agricultural runoff, upstream
wastewater discharges, road crossings). The assessment is available at
410 Riverside Dr, Cedar Ridge.

HOW IS MY WATER TREATED?
------------------------
Conventional treatment at the Cedar Ridge Water Treatment Plant: coagulation,
flocculation, sedimentation, dual-media filtration, chlorine disinfection and
pH adjustment with sodium hydroxide for corrosion control. Finished water
travels through a 16-inch transmission main to the Hilltop Booster Pump
Station (PS-3) and the 1.0-million-gallon Summit Elevated Tank.

  2025 average day demand ............ 4.8 MGD
  2025 peak day demand ............... 8.3 MGD (August 21, 2025)
  Total water delivered .............. 1,752 million gallons

